# Click-through tour of the API.
#
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), boot the stack
# (docker compose up --build -d --wait), then click "Send Request" above each request,
# top to bottom. Later requests reuse ids and versions from earlier responses, so
# nothing needs copying. Give the worker a few seconds between steps 1 and 2.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Create a tenant: 202, tenant "provisioning", task "deploy" / "accepted"
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{"slug": "demo-{{$randomInt 100000 999999}}", "name": "Demo Corp"}

### 2. Get it: "active" at version 2 once the worker has deployed it
# @name get
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/{{create.response.body.$.tenant.id}}

### 3. Its tasks, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/{{create.response.body.$.tenant.id}}/tasks

### 4. The deploy task on its own
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{create.response.body.$.task.id}}

### 5. Rename it: 202, "updating". Uses the version from step 2, so send step 2
# First send step 2 (until it shows "active"); otherwise this goes out with no version: 400.
# @name update
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/{{create.response.body.$.tenant.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Demo Corp Renamed", "version": {{get.response.body.$.version}}}

### 6. Same PATCH again with the version step 2 returned, now stale: 409 tenant_version_conflict
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/{{create.response.body.$.tenant.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Lost Update", "version": {{get.response.body.$.version}}}

### 7. Delete it (re-run step 2 first until it is "active" again): 202, "destroying"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/{{create.response.body.$.tenant.id}}

### 8. Its slug stays taken, even once destroyed: 409 tenant_already_exists
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{"slug": "{{create.response.body.$.tenant.slug}}", "name": "Copycat"}

### --- Listing, filtering and paging -----------------------------------------------

### Active tenants, two per page; pass "next_cursor" as ?cursor= for the next page
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants?status=active&limit=2

### Failed tasks of any tenant
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks?status=failed

### Destroy tasks of the tenant from step 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks?tenant_id={{create.response.body.$.tenant.id}}&type=destroy

### --- Errors: every one has the same {"error": {"code", "message", "details"}} shape ---

### 400 validation_failed: slug breaks the pattern, name is blank
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{"slug": "Not A Slug", "name": ""}

### 404 tenant_not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 404 task_not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 400 validation_failed: limit out of range
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants?limit=500

### --- Health ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Readiness: database and broker both reachable
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz
